00:17:23.699 --> 00:17:25.133
It's really hot. We
went up a mountain,

00:17:33.878 --> 00:17:36.238
and now we're going downhill.

00:17:38.800 --> 00:17:40.266
3K, actually it's quite

00:17:59.836 --> 00:18:00.533
fast to get to the road.

00:18:06.713 --> 00:18:10.868
It's all about driving
on highways,

00:18:16.448 --> 00:18:19.548
it's about driving on super steep hills,
now we're on A1.

00:18:19.548 --> 00:18:20.400
Add a bottle of colored
water (actually,

00:18:32.148 --> 00:18:34.966
it's a drinkable bottle of Kettrium).
Don't drink it.

00:18:37.733 --> 00:18:38.448
Eating a small piece of watermelon

00:18:41.968 --> 00:18:43.067
is quite accurate. 4.6K

00:18:45.466 --> 00:18:48.848
The trail leading up to the mountain

00:18:48.848 --> 00:18:50.233
is a relatively long 10km section.

00:18:55.699 --> 00:18:57.242
It's really hot; the sun is out

00:19:03.966 --> 00:19:04.700
and the waterfall is in full bloom.

00:19:10.453 --> 00:19:12.324
It's quite slippery;
I was thinking of saying

00:19:15.600 --> 00:19:17.998
this is some kind of small
suburban mountain.

00:19:18.578 --> 00:19:22.198
As a result, because it was too dense and it kept raining,
this area...

00:19:22.198 --> 00:19:25.838
The vegetation is incredibly thick,

00:19:25.838 --> 00:19:28.533
the branches are quite dense,
it looks like we really need to cross the stream.

00:19:30.300 --> 00:19:32.300
(I really don't want to

00:19:36.358 --> 00:19:37.133
step in water) MDFKKKKK

00:19:37.234 --> 00:19:38.000
There are lots of tree trunks

00:19:38.044 --> 00:19:39.347
and lots of grass!

00:19:46.232 --> 00:19:47.536
(Inner despair) It's hopeless,

00:19:48.258 --> 00:19:52.158
it's hopeless,
if this continues...

00:19:52.158 --> 00:19:54.666
This is hopeless,

00:20:46.666 --> 00:20:50.148
hopeless, it's so uncomfortable,
so annoying.

00:20:50.148 --> 00:20:53.699
I'm so annoyed,

00:21:12.529 --> 00:21:13.711
my feet are covered in sand,
and he's being attacked (chased).

00:21:14.200 --> 00:21:15.998
Luckily, we have the BD
Scepter, so we're

00:21:15.998 --> 00:21:20.698
not afraid of Thai dogs!
Thai dogs are cute!

00:21:20.698 --> 00:21:23.038
It just wants to play with you,
so don't play with it (?).

00:21:23.038 --> 00:21:26.838
That's good, just walk a little
further away and run faster.

00:21:26.838 --> 00:21:29.200
They were still chasing after them

00:21:30.066 --> 00:21:31.398
as they climbed the mountain.

00:21:33.908 --> 00:21:38.028
It's quite steep here;
there should be two peaks.

00:21:38.028 --> 00:21:42.028
One goes down halfway and
then goes up again.

00:21:42.028 --> 00:21:45.028
It's less than 5,

00:21:45.028 --> 00:21:47.299
000 km to the supply station, probably more than 4,
000 km, which means climbing mountains.

00:21:56.908 --> 00:21:59.633
"Tauru,

00:22:00.583 --> 00:22:03.191
Koukun Coffee"
- Tested! He'll take your picture whether you tell him or not, hahaha.

00:22:03.500 --> 00:22:05.626
We're going uphill now,

00:22:22.278 --> 00:22:23.366
it's chilly.

00:22:25.033 --> 00:22:25.766
Hot Thai fabric

00:22:25.766 --> 00:22:27.278
strips

00:22:27.278 --> 00:22:30.098
Running beast cloth strips cloth strips
cloth strips are all cloth strips

00:22:30.098 --> 00:22:34.038
It is absolutely certain that
it is impossible to get lost.

00:22:34.038 --> 00:22:36.978
Yes, it's definitely
your problem.

00:22:36.978 --> 00:22:39.938
There are just too many,
too many questions from Taiwanese people.

00:22:39.938 --> 00:22:43.198
I'd like to offer some advice to people
in Taiwan: please don't skimp on

00:22:43.198 --> 00:22:45.258
the running strips. I think trail running
isn't about finding the route.

00:22:45.258 --> 00:22:47.438
If it's not orienteering or hide
-and-seek,

00:22:47.438 --> 00:22:50.738
trail runners don't need
to make any judgments.

00:22:50.738 --> 00:22:53.398
Running a full 50K lap
is already considered

00:22:53.398 --> 00:22:56.758
a medium
-distance course for them.

00:22:56.758 --> 00:22:58.266
Don't skimp on the cost of this cloth strip
if you really need to tie a lot of cloth.

00:22:58.266 --> 00:23:00.034
I wasn't talking about
anyone (quickly clarify).

00:23:00.066 --> 00:23:03.838
I think this is how competitions
should be done.

00:23:03.838 --> 00:23:05.978
Don't skimp on fabric
strips; reuse them.

00:23:05.978 --> 00:23:10.458
There are many guidelines like this.

00:23:10.458 --> 00:23:12.438
If the path is a little unclear,
use an arrow.

00:23:12.438 --> 00:23:14.766
It's very clear
that the right side

00:23:24.300 --> 00:23:25.600
is again covered in super
-shaky fabric.

00:23:28.658 --> 00:23:33.698
It looks like we're
on an exploration route,

00:23:33.698 --> 00:23:34.566
then a steep climb that looks like we've
cut through this bamboo forest.

00:23:38.666 --> 00:23:39.933
My arm can only be raised this far,

00:23:39.993 --> 00:23:40.801
it's too steep.

00:23:59.621 --> 00:24:01.299
So tired~ It's so steep~
We've passed the highest

00:24:13.248 --> 00:24:16.228
point and need to prepare
to descend to A1.

00:24:16.228 --> 00:24:17.433
It should download to A2 13.

00:24:17.557 --> 00:24:20.000
5K, OK.

00:24:20.000 --> 00:24:24.288
Then there's a very technical
downhill section,

00:24:24.288 --> 00:24:26.468
but I'm too scared to run on it.

00:24:26.468 --> 00:24:30.708
Because the stones here are
unpredictable; it's

00:24:30.708 --> 00:24:33.128
impossible to know how such
stones could exist.

00:24:33.128 --> 00:24:35.348
Some can run,
but because of their feet...

00:24:35.348 --> 00:24:38.533
Because of that,

00:24:39.035 --> 00:24:40.553
I won't run anymore, OK? (cluck cluck cluck cluck
cluck cluck cluck cluck cluck cluck cluck cluck)

00:24:57.350 --> 00:24:58.200
Super Ice

00:25:03.807 --> 00:25:04.633
Milk

00:25:11.679 --> 00:25:12.594
Pectin water should also

00:25:14.800 --> 00:25:15.800
be served with ice cubes.

00:25:15.800 --> 00:25:17.478
Fill the container with water

00:25:18.838 --> 00:25:20.033
and add lots of ice.

00:25:32.120 --> 00:25:35.335
The highway ends and you have to turn
onto a mountain path (right?).

00:25:41.838 --> 00:25:42.833
It's super steep. Why is that? Because
there's no footwork involved.

00:25:50.434 --> 00:25:51.808
Why use a staff? Because
there are no steps

00:25:51.808 --> 00:25:56.708
or stones; the ground is very flat.

00:25:56.708 --> 00:25:59.100
No, it's just a dirt

00:26:14.992 --> 00:26:17.133
slope (very steep!).

00:26:38.368 --> 00:26:40.966
Extremely technical steep,

00:26:41.044 --> 00:26:43.066
incredibly steep!

00:26:46.966 --> 00:26:47.968
Be careful, there are thorns here,
so don't scratch them.

00:26:47.968 --> 00:26:51.966
There are also some ropes.

00:26:55.033 --> 00:26:55.928
The ridgeline has a low elevation,

00:26:55.928 --> 00:26:59.108
ranging from 300 to 310 meters.

00:26:59.108 --> 00:27:01.608
320 should be preparing to go down soon,
theoretically.

00:27:01.608 --> 00:27:05.766
mountainous suburbs

00:27:06.648 --> 00:27:08.066
of Thailand

00:27:08.066 --> 00:27:09.533
So tired, oh my god, oh my

00:27:11.981 --> 00:27:14.028
god, oh my god, oh my god!

00:27:14.028 --> 00:27:14.800
The reclining Buddha appears

00:27:18.566 --> 00:27:20.428
to have been chopped down.

00:27:20.428 --> 00:27:22.808
It was cut down; this place should

00:27:22.808 --> 00:27:23.600
be covered with bamboo.

00:27:54.678 --> 00:27:56.300
Looks like we can set up camp now,

00:27:58.733 --> 00:28:00.233
after wading through the water.

00:28:02.308 --> 00:28:05.648
Thailand's Tiger and Leopard Duo, the Thailand Tiger and Leopard Cross
-Country Race!

00:28:05.648 --> 00:28:07.968
I didn't go to any water
sports in Taiwan this year,

00:28:07.968 --> 00:28:09.666
so I came to Thailand instead.

00:28:09.666 --> 00:28:11.028
The third batch of electrolyte
capsules

00:28:13.900 --> 00:28:15.728
is almost at the last mountain.

00:28:16.328 --> 00:28:21.588
Down to A3, 23.

00:28:28.000 --> 00:28:31.000
5K, now almost 20K. Let me tell you, thank goodness I had trekking poles,
otherwise I really would be done for.

00:28:49.378 --> 00:28:51.738
(When I first encountered) 100K runners,
I noticed their bib numbers were different.

00:28:51.738 --> 00:28:55.638
He told me: I'm in the top 10,
I'm totally...

00:28:55.638 --> 00:28:57.078
I don't know,
I originally thought I had probably...

00:28:57.078 --> 00:29:00.638
More than 20 because after deducting
the elite players,

00:29:00.638 --> 00:29:03.658
some local players, and foreigners,

00:29:03.658 --> 00:29:05.718
I think 20
-something is about right, but he said I was ahead of him.

00:29:05.718 --> 00:29:08.298
Only 10 of them said I might
be able to catch up.

00:29:10.018 --> 00:29:12.858
Actually, I didn't expect
him to say that I

00:29:12.858 --> 00:29:17.638
couldn't slack off,
OMG, I'm nervous.

00:29:18.278 --> 00:29:20.538
Being nervous almost caused me to fall to my death.
Let's not be nervous.

00:29:21.018 --> 00:29:21.500
Don't be nervous,

00:29:23.478 --> 00:29:26.338
I'll teach you a Thai phrase
for "how to bargain."

00:29:26.338 --> 00:29:29.538
Jin Jin = Very Much,
and Ma Ma = Too Much.

00:29:29.538 --> 00:29:33.618
Then if it's too expensive,

00:29:33.618 --> 00:29:34.933
just say "next time"
or "this one".

00:29:37.323 --> 00:29:39.538
It's very expensive.

00:29:39.538 --> 00:29:41.618
"Gold" and "cursing"
are used in slightly different ways.

00:29:41.618 --> 00:29:43.698
Jin Jin is used in water (very appropriate).
Most of the criticism is directed at me.

00:29:43.698 --> 00:29:48.876
Used in "Lor", "PengLorMaMa"
means "I'm so handsome".

00:29:48.899 --> 00:29:49.766
You could say that we generally

00:29:49.766 --> 00:29:51.420
don't compliment boys XDD

00:29:51.533 --> 00:29:52.518
So just remember Kun =
you are very upright,

00:29:52.518 --> 00:29:56.518
you are very upright.

00:29:56.518 --> 00:29:59.708
I'll come with you for a trail
running race in Khao Yai (?)

00:30:00.166 --> 00:30:02.099
He would be dumbfounded by the

00:06:32.725 --> 00:06:33.600
high
-profile inspection.

00:08:50.535 --> 00:08:51.800
Hey (actually yelling),

00:22:20.995 --> 00:22:22.161
let's start a fire here
(it's super hot).

00:09:34.583 --> 00:09:36.028
Eyes asleep is in

00:05:58.646 --> 00:06:01.122
Hokkien Province

00:30:02.110 --> 00:30:04.849
It's too expensive,

00:30:04.849 --> 00:30:07.090
so I need a cheaper price.
= ni nor dai mai

00:30:07.090 --> 00:30:10.410
ni nor = cheap ni nor

00:30:10.410 --> 00:30:13.370
= slightly cheaper

00:30:13.395 --> 00:30:15.835
Is it cheap? "Dai mai" means "Is it
okay?" "Dai" means "yes".

00:30:16.395 --> 00:30:17.955
mai = ma? (interrogative sentence)
dai mai = is it okay?

00:30:18.555 --> 00:30:22.535
Hurry up and get to the finish line,
dai mai? (Mai dai = no)

00:30:22.535 --> 00:30:25.675
Thai Language Lesson Lian Pa Sam Thai (Learn Thai)
- End!

00:30:26.155 --> 00:30:28.835
Okay, so we should go
downhill now, right?

00:30:28.835 --> 00:30:30.155
It's not downhill yet,

00:30:30.155 --> 00:30:32.775
the top 10 are useless now,
we need half of them.

00:30:32.775 --> 00:30:35.695
Not there yet,
only about 20km left. Keep going!

00:30:35.695 --> 00:30:36.300
Dog! It's been almost
to A3 for ages,

00:31:14.901 --> 00:31:20.085
it's been almost 4 hours already,
and it's still not done.

00:31:20.085 --> 00:31:20.999
The water in Thailand,

00:31:31.100 --> 00:31:33.266
which is 23km away,
is incredibly cold and amazing.

00:31:37.333 --> 00:31:39.133
There are braised eggs to eat,

00:31:49.333 --> 00:31:51.351
but they might make you look
like a watermelon demon.

00:31:53.966 --> 00:31:56.133
OMG, the Nile? That's
an exaggeration.

00:32:02.945 --> 00:32:07.345
Wannan Creek,
the Andong Army crossing the creek...

00:32:14.266 --> 00:32:16.325
The TNF100, I haven't finished it yet,
it's so much

00:32:16.325 --> 00:32:20.265
fun! It's tough,
but it really is like a jungle!

00:32:20.645 --> 00:32:22.985
No joke, it includes all sorts of rainforest,
scree, uphill,

00:32:22.985 --> 00:32:27.545
downhill, stream tracing,
and river crossings.

00:32:27.545 --> 00:32:31.385
You can camp here if you're
really cool.

00:32:31.385 --> 00:32:33.645
If it's super heat
-resistant,

00:32:34.145 --> 00:32:36.305
we could camp here. Everyone's almost dead,
so we've used it all up. I'm almost dead too.

00:32:41.100 --> 00:32:43.945
Ron is hot,

00:32:44.505 --> 00:32:45.666
Ron is hot!

00:32:45.666 --> 00:32:47.825
After logging,

00:32:47.825 --> 00:32:52.945
the planted forests are arranged in
a very straight but regular pattern.

00:32:52.945 --> 00:32:55.865
So in Taiwan,
they plant cedar trees now.

00:32:55.865 --> 00:32:59.145
Almost everyone involved
logging; it was

00:33:00.225 --> 00:33:01.299
a pretty cool road back in the day.

00:33:02.800 --> 00:33:05.845
50km runners can

00:33:05.845 --> 00:33:08.400
use swimming

00:33:27.015 --> 00:33:30.315
Thai ruins, probably a former village,
now deserted.

00:33:30.315 --> 00:33:34.466
Continue, doggy!

00:33:34.466 --> 00:33:36.466
This past

00:33:36.466 --> 00:33:40.145
(Speechless with fright) We
should use a swimming pool,

00:33:41.932 --> 00:33:44.519
right?

00:33:58.200 --> 00:33:59.887
It's Beibiao Mansion,
right? (There's a landmark nearby.)

00:34:05.095 --> 00:34:06.066
Don't let it get washed away!
Prepare four packets of pectin

00:34:22.955 --> 00:34:25.666
in the second tube.
Now add water for the second half.

00:34:30.233 --> 00:34:31.211
I don't dare eat the meat bun (I
don't know what the criticism is,

00:34:32.366 --> 00:34:33.666
but I still asked him to
criticize it for me).

00:34:35.294 --> 00:34:37.705
It looks like a place
for horseback riding;

00:34:38.445 --> 00:34:40.866
there are quite a few horses.

00:34:42.300 --> 00:34:43.233
MDFK main road so.......very
collapsing,

00:34:46.099 --> 00:34:48.837
about to heat to death

00:34:48.899 --> 00:34:49.733
30K, super

00:34:49.733 --> 00:34:51.699
sunny

00:34:52.285 --> 00:34:54.625
The A4 is about to turn
into the A5; it should

00:34:54.625 --> 00:34:56.705
consist of some gentle slopes,
not steep ones.

00:34:56.705 --> 00:35:01.005
The steepest part is the last section from A5 to
A6 (which involves an ascent of 1500 meters).

00:35:01.265 --> 00:35:04.485
The highway was really tough; I
wonder what the temperature was.

00:35:04.485 --> 00:35:05.566
40 degrees, drink

00:35:06.899 --> 00:35:08.433
some Kai Te Li

00:35:14.057 --> 00:35:15.566
It's as hot as Kenting
(it looks so

00:35:22.538 --> 00:35:23.800
cool watching others
collect sticks!).

00:35:23.800 --> 00:35:24.633
The title of "King of
Wooden Sticks" is his!

00:35:29.835 --> 00:35:33.177
Hurry up and get to A5,
I've run out of Thai words!

00:35:33.200 --> 00:35:38.275
I just ran out of vocabulary and
asked him (sǎam sìp kâo = 39K)

00:35:38.275 --> 00:35:43.433
KM told me he didn't know,

00:35:43.488 --> 00:35:44.933
damn it, it's noon now.

00:35:46.099 --> 00:35:47.100
Oh no! (??) I'm going to die at
12:30 (My Taiwanese is terrible,

00:35:50.815 --> 00:35:53.466
haha)

00:36:19.005 --> 00:36:22.045
To navigate through these "miscellaneous
fish" routes,

00:36:22.045 --> 00:36:25.145
one must navigate through the weeds and miscellaneous fish;
these are called "miscellaneous fish routes."

00:36:25.145 --> 00:36:28.265
It's just about accumulating mileage gradually,
but nothing serious.

00:36:28.265 --> 00:36:30.033
The shelter is

00:36:30.899 --> 00:36:31.666
at station A5!

00:36:35.333 --> 00:36:37.266
(At this stop, we unloaded our equipment,
organized our gear, and changed the camera battery.)

00:36:41.695 --> 00:36:44.000
Looks like...
it'll be a disaster (XD) (Watermelon

00:36:48.415 --> 00:36:49.881
King is still eating watermelon)

00:36:52.405 --> 00:36:56.333
Ice? That's ridiculous! (And
grass jelly too!) You're

00:36:56.333 --> 00:36:58.766
heat
-resistant enough to eat instant noodles.

00:37:04.365 --> 00:37:09.225
The last mountain, the dog is about to get heatstroke,
his skin feels a little numb.

00:37:09.225 --> 00:37:13.965
I just used a lot of ice water
to cool the ice cream down,

00:37:13.965 --> 00:37:16.885
but I don't dare eat it because
I think it's too hard.

00:37:16.885 --> 00:37:20.585
We're heading to
a distance of 45km,

00:37:20.585 --> 00:37:21.766
which is approximately 6km.

00:37:25.632 --> 00:37:32.025
It should be the last slope on the mountain trail,
the highest point today is 400 meters.

00:37:32.025 --> 00:37:35.865
I didn't reach 400m today.

00:37:35.865 --> 00:37:42.185
My highest today was 330. The last peak was really tough.
This race was pretty bad.

00:37:42.185 --> 00:37:45.145
Running at an altitude of 100
-400 meters is very hot, but this number makes you feel...

00:37:45.145 --> 00:37:47.825
It seems like the pressure isn't that great,
so I won't say anything today.

00:37:47.825 --> 00:37:52.345
Going from 700
-800 to 2000 is terrifying. The FXT competition is alright,

00:37:52.345 --> 00:37:56.065
it happens very quickly.

00:37:56.065 --> 00:37:58.965
His segment will never exceed 300,
so 300 is actually...

00:37:58.965 --> 00:38:03.705
These are all foods that
everyone can eat,

00:38:03.705 --> 00:38:09.385
but it's too hot to be in the sun;
it really might cause a health problem.

00:38:10.333 --> 00:38:12.100
ㄍㄧㄣ骂ㄍㄧㄣ骂ㄍㄧㄣ骂ㄍㄧㄣ骂

00:38:12.100 --> 00:38:14.185
If you pass by him,

00:38:14.185 --> 00:38:15.666
he'll say to you: "You're
really good at cursing!"

00:38:15.666 --> 00:38:17.033
I'm really good

00:38:17.033 --> 00:38:18.362
at scolding you!

00:38:18.451 --> 00:38:22.500
I'm forcing you to
repeat after me! (Sigh)

00:38:25.466 --> 00:38:26.533
Why is it still turning
into a highway gg?

00:38:30.733 --> 00:38:34.765
Another path full of fish and weeds,
this path is corn.

00:38:34.765 --> 00:38:37.185
It should be corn,

00:38:37.185 --> 00:38:40.900
but I don't know what it is;
it looks like a small bean tree.

00:38:41.733 --> 00:38:42.585
This BD (Black Diamond) trekking pole has a quick
-release buckle; pressing

00:38:42.585 --> 00:38:47.625
it down to release and then locking
it securely keeps the pole in place.

00:38:47.625 --> 00:38:50.299
Holding it like this,
is the wristband on the other hand not included?

00:38:51.066 --> 00:38:52.285
I think it's quite useful; it's
very lightweight and supports

00:38:52.285 --> 00:38:55.165
the strength of your hands,
making it suitable for trail running.

00:38:55.165 --> 00:38:57.085
Hiking is an option,
but I would feel that hiking...

00:38:57.085 --> 00:38:59.225
It should be possible to adjust the
downhill section to be a bit longer.

00:38:59.225 --> 00:39:03.625
So this is for trail running;
it can't be adjusted,

00:39:03.625 --> 00:39:07.165
it's a fixed length. But today
I'm using a pole pack, and...

00:39:07.165 --> 00:39:09.165
I wasn't collecting them because
I was mostly carrying a cane.

00:39:09.165 --> 00:39:11.765
Then I don't need a cane,
I can just hold this.

00:39:11.765 --> 00:39:12.633
Untie it like this,

00:39:13.366 --> 00:39:14.133
untie it like this

00:39:16.400 --> 00:39:21.245
Unfasten and then fasten back on,

00:39:21.412 --> 00:39:22.499
OK, doggy!

00:39:23.066 --> 00:39:25.765
Now, just climb the last one smoothly,
and you'll be fine once you get in (the mountain path).

00:39:25.765 --> 00:39:28.005
I shouldn't get heatstroke
because my skin is already...

00:39:28.005 --> 00:39:32.285
I felt numb from the heatstroke,
and this was the only one left, so I just had to hold on.

00:39:32.285 --> 00:39:35.566
Steadily climbing mountains is my specialty
(a confident statement from myself).

00:39:46.595 --> 00:39:49.266
The path wasn't very clear; it seemed
like hardly anyone was walking on it.

00:39:56.545 --> 00:40:00.321
The highest point should be around 440M,
then stop at W1, the last checkpoint.

00:40:00.466 --> 00:40:01.400
2K down, back to the
finish line, finally

00:40:01.400 --> 00:40:03.500
this hot game is about to end.

00:40:03.500 --> 00:40:04.566
Take it slow and

00:40:04.566 --> 00:40:06.333
walk slowly.

00:40:09.581 --> 00:40:12.000
Come out! Eat the last bag of unripe mangoes,
eat one directly.

00:40:12.766 --> 00:40:14.866
Green mango,

00:40:15.661 --> 00:40:18.166
even when frozen,
can be torn open without spilling.

00:40:19.566 --> 00:40:20.433
No water needed! Awesome! I'll

00:40:23.300 --> 00:40:25.985
finish it right away!

00:40:25.985 --> 00:40:27.899
W1 quickly passed by (I lingered

00:40:30.740 --> 00:40:32.221
at the last stop for a bit).

00:40:38.905 --> 00:40:40.266
Running downhill along

00:40:43.460 --> 00:40:45.125
that road now

00:40:45.125 --> 00:40:48.699
At an altitude of 449 meters,
is this the diving platform (??)?

00:40:50.598 --> 00:40:51.166
Dog! The mountain bike

00:40:51.166 --> 00:40:52.985
area should be...

00:40:52.985 --> 00:40:55.500
The car is flying downhill,

00:40:55.500 --> 00:40:58.633
so this way you won't crash into trees or get
hurt (do I need to demonstrate this myself?).

00:40:59.325 --> 00:41:00.433
Four
-wheel drive (?) I'm

00:41:06.314 --> 00:41:07.574
so excited right now!

00:41:07.625 --> 00:41:10.765
Although I was almost suffering from heatstroke
from the sound of the main venue,

00:41:10.765 --> 00:41:13.525
I feel okay right now,
though my legs are quite sore.

00:41:15.133 --> 00:41:18.325
So almost twisted not to mess
with the words I think

00:41:18.325 --> 00:41:20.565
The shoes are excellent for road running;
they have a good thickness,

00:41:20.565 --> 00:41:23.905
providing cushioning and elasticity.

00:41:23.905 --> 00:41:26.645
At my speed,
these shoes are really quite suitable.

00:41:26.645 --> 00:41:29.205
I think it's fine for intermediate and lower
-intermediate levels.

00:41:30.025 --> 00:41:33.568
I recommend these Enduris
4 shoes to everyone.

00:41:33.633 --> 00:41:35.085
I think the anti
-slip properties

00:41:35.085 --> 00:41:36.066
are even better than Enduris 3.

00:41:36.066 --> 00:41:37.405
I think its last is somewhere in the

00:41:37.405 --> 00:41:39.925
middle; it's also pointed.

00:41:39.925 --> 00:41:42.805
I found it quite comfortable to run
around in a space with enough room.

00:41:42.805 --> 00:41:45.085
But today, the sand just keeps coming
in and it's uncomfortable.

00:41:45.085 --> 00:41:46.405
But I think every shoe
would be affected

00:41:46.405 --> 00:41:48.033
because the water was just too dirty.

00:41:48.033 --> 00:41:49.945
The water bladder vest is excellent;
it doesn't wobble

00:41:49.945 --> 00:41:52.825
at all and is very stable. However,
I think this...

00:41:52.825 --> 00:41:55.545
The location (where the water bottle is placed) is quite difficult
to fit in; it's not easy to insert because...

00:41:55.545 --> 00:41:57.685
It was inserted very forcefully,
so it was very stable.

00:41:57.685 --> 00:42:00.585
I discovered that this tent bag can also hold a soft water bottle
when I insert another water bottle at the bottom back.

00:42:00.585 --> 00:42:03.305
I can also insert two 1L water
bottles into my back,

00:42:03.305 --> 00:42:05.445
plus a pectin solution, and then...

00:42:05.445 --> 00:42:07.465
Prepare another pectin bottle; since
we haven't filled them with water

00:42:07.465 --> 00:42:08.685
yet, we'll have a total of four
soft water bottles to replace them.

00:42:08.685 --> 00:42:10.633
Extremely useful when
you're halfway

00:42:10.716 --> 00:42:13.585
between supply stations A and B.

00:42:13.585 --> 00:42:15.885
Drink a bottle of, say, 10K.

00:42:15.885 --> 00:42:18.028
The middle 10K is 5K for
drinking a can of water,

00:42:18.066 --> 00:42:19.825
and the remaining 5K must exceed 5K.

00:42:19.825 --> 00:42:22.145
Then take out another
bottle of water,

00:42:22.145 --> 00:42:25.025
and you'll definitely
not run out of water.

00:42:25.025 --> 00:42:27.085
I'll drink half of the pectin water to replenish my balance,
then drink the other half to replenish my balance (it takes time).

00:42:27.085 --> 00:42:29.125
Another advantage of Thailand,
in my opinion, is that it has a lot of ice.

00:42:30.668 --> 00:42:33.425
Today, I didn't get up because I had no teeth,
and there were a few stops where I drank ice water.

00:42:33.425 --> 00:42:36.865
Ice cubes, ice water, then bite them with your mouth,
hold them in your hand and stuff them into your stomach.

00:42:36.865 --> 00:42:39.145
The large ice cream for the breasts,

00:42:39.145 --> 00:42:42.200
back, and neck is incredibly useful!

00:42:45.251 --> 00:42:49.761
Seeing the lake, it's just like in Hong Kong (I hadn't
yet connected it to the lake at the venue).

00:42:55.525 --> 00:42:57.333
It's almost here!!! (So

00:42:59.666 --> 00:43:00.766
touching!) So moved TT

00:43:09.183 --> 00:43:12.100
(Finally, all I wanted to do
when I got here was rest....)

00:43:15.347 --> 00:43:17.833
(Check out my results
at Garmin!) (The

00:43:17.833 --> 00:43:19.366
race gives out a lot
of meal vouchers!)

00:43:30.115 --> 00:43:32.066
Water, gold, gold! (This is the
only phrase I use in Thailand!)

00:43:38.233 --> 00:43:40.775
(A children's cross
-country

00:43:41.443 --> 00:43:42.743
race) (Outrageous) 100K finisher

00:43:46.733 --> 00:43:48.033
It looks like it's
better than HYROX...

00:43:52.615 --> 00:43:57.135
We're back at the TNF100

00:43:57.135 --> 00:43:58.735
event the next day now.

00:43:58.735 --> 00:44:01.495
I was a bit tired yesterday,

00:44:01.495 --> 00:44:04.795
so I didn't continue sharing
my thoughts on the competition.

00:44:04.795 --> 00:44:07.295
Now, let me share my thoughts on this event.
I think it's really noisy right now.

00:44:07.295 --> 00:44:09.499
There was a lot of Thai writing,

00:44:09.499 --> 00:44:10.666
and that person kept saying
"Thai Zuja"?

00:44:10.666 --> 00:44:12.775
This tournament in Thailand
is definitely

00:44:12.775 --> 00:44:14.955
worth participating in
because I think...

00:44:14.955 --> 00:44:17.055
It's not high in altitude,

00:44:17.055 --> 00:44:20.755
but the terrain is very varied, involving crossing streams,
tracing streams, and crossing rivers.

00:44:20.755 --> 00:44:22.955
The scene was incredibly exaggerated.

00:44:22.955 --> 00:44:25.515
The slope is extremely steep.

00:44:25.515 --> 00:44:28.155
And the route was indeed
very primitive,

00:44:28.155 --> 00:44:30.035
because that route was
almost entirely my...

00:44:30.035 --> 00:44:32.095
They believed that what it
produced was not ordinary.

00:44:32.095 --> 00:44:33.915
It seems we didn't see
yesterday's game.

00:44:33.915 --> 00:44:36.695
Any mountaineer like
this only competes.

00:44:36.695 --> 00:44:38.855
For many locals,

00:44:38.855 --> 00:44:40.855
Thailand is a popular
vacation destination.

00:44:40.855 --> 00:44:42.535
Most of the competitors who come

00:44:42.535 --> 00:44:45.735
to this track are local Thais.

00:44:45.735 --> 00:44:48.235
Yesterday's 100km run
was really exaggerated.

00:44:48.235 --> 00:44:51.135
I checked his record
and his marathon time

00:44:51.135 --> 00:44:53.400
It takes 2 hours and 45 minutes,

00:44:53.400 --> 00:44:55.766
super fast! Locals = Kun (Thai)

00:44:55.800 --> 00:44:57.695
That's why he can run so fast.

00:44:57.695 --> 00:45:00.315
Thankfully, I didn't listen
to the instructions

00:45:00.315 --> 00:45:02.015
on the track to chase
after the top ten.

00:45:02.015 --> 00:45:04.415
My suggestion is to run
at my speed and pace.

00:45:04.415 --> 00:45:07.875
Overall, the condition was a
slight case of heatstroke,

00:45:07.875 --> 00:45:11.515
but it was okay because I didn't
go to the hospital.

00:45:11.515 --> 00:45:14.055
I've been constantly
noticing what problems

00:45:14.055 --> 00:45:16.335
or discomforts my body might have.

00:45:16.335 --> 00:45:18.215
Hurry up and make adjustments
and improvements. Does this,

00:45:18.215 --> 00:45:22.275
along with my early game,
count as the early game?

00:45:22.275 --> 00:45:26.155
This is what my training was
like before my injury.

00:45:26.155 --> 00:45:28.415
I think it's about accumulating some
elevation gain by running a few steps.

00:45:28.415 --> 00:45:30.295
It's all about practice; if you practice,
you won't get it. If you want to...

00:45:30.295 --> 00:45:34.915
When hiking the TNF100 in Thailand, you absolutely must use trekking poles.
I think 50K is a good starting point.

00:45:34.915 --> 00:45:37.655
If you're not an elite runner
and aren't a great runner,

00:45:37.655 --> 00:45:42.355
using trekking poles is a very cost
-effective option.

00:45:42.355 --> 00:45:44.295
Cooling down is a strategy
because in this environment

00:45:44.295 --> 00:45:47.909
you must find ways to
cool yourself down.

00:45:47.933 --> 00:45:50.075
There are ice cubes at every
refueling station,

00:45:50.075 --> 00:45:51.995
but having ice cubes is one thing,
but how do you use them?

00:45:51.995 --> 00:45:54.055
Ice cubes are used when
you go for a shower,

00:45:54.055 --> 00:45:56.875
when you cross a stream,
or when you rinse your body with ice.

00:45:56.875 --> 00:45:59.775
The front is plugged,

00:45:59.775 --> 00:46:01.635
the back is plugged, soft water is plugged in,
the mouth is plugged in, and the hand is plugged in because of its ice.

00:46:01.635 --> 00:46:04.395
The pieces are really big
and don't melt easily.

00:46:04.395 --> 00:46:07.815
First hold it in your mouth (??)
First hold it in your hand

00:46:07.815 --> 00:46:10.255
If you're good at swallowing,

00:46:10.255 --> 00:46:12.495
you can swallow smaller pieces and then put them in your mouth,
like a chipmunk.

00:46:12.495 --> 00:46:14.775
I think a few of these are also very
useful for cooling down the mouth.

00:46:14.775 --> 00:46:18.995
And the neck core,
big ice milk and stuffing

00:46:18.995 --> 00:46:21.635
There was a cooling sensation
inside my stomach.

00:46:21.635 --> 00:46:24.135
Without these ice cubes, I think I am

00:46:24.135 --> 00:46:27.515
Strategies for running out of supplies,
how to replenish electrolytes, like me

00:46:27.515 --> 00:46:29.675
Yesterday, I added about 20
more (electrolytic) units.

00:46:29.675 --> 00:46:32.175
Every hour, and I'm shortening the time, it's about 45
-50 minutes.

00:46:32.175 --> 00:46:34.415
Since you'll need
to take one dose,

00:46:34.415 --> 00:46:37.515
you should distribute the six doses (of capsules) over a seven
-and-a-half-hour period.

00:46:37.515 --> 00:46:40.195
Although finishing yesterday
was quite painful,

00:46:40.195 --> 00:46:41.695
especially the road race,
it was still a bit tough.

00:46:41.695 --> 00:46:44.655
Even under the blazing sun,
my [interest/attention] remains undiminished.

00:46:44.655 --> 00:46:46.099
I love Thailand (after all,
it's my home overseas &gt;///&lt;)

00:46:46.099 --> 00:46:48.815
If I had the chance,

00:46:48.815 --> 00:46:52.215
I would really like to compete
in Thailand again.

00:46:52.215 --> 00:46:54.075
It also includes my excellent experience
going to Chiang Mai last year,

00:46:54.075 --> 00:46:57.015
and this time it's Koai.

00:46:57.015 --> 00:47:01.935
Regional competitions are
also very worthwhile.

00:47:01.935 --> 00:47:03.600
That's all for today's video.

00:47:03.600 --> 00:47:04.195
Did you enjoy my video?

00:47:05.566 --> 00:47:06.805
I'm Hiker CP.

00:47:06.873 --> 00:47:08.800
See you on the mountain next time!

00:47:08.815 --> 00:47:09.433
Bye
-bye, the

00:35:48.569 --> 00:35:50.648
sun is high!

